(Government programs permit stacking \(combining multiple grants\), but impose strict legal caps to prevent duplicate billing for identical) Tj
T* (costs. Under U.S. Uniform Guidance \(2 CFR 200\) and Canadian Treasury Board Policy, total combined government assistance cannot) Tj
T* (exceed 75% to 80% of eligible project cost.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
45.354330708661422 698.4569291338582389 Td
(THE OPTIMAL STACKING FORMULA: \(1\) Use direct wage subsidies to offset 50–70% of junior/co-op hiring payroll, \(2\) Deduct the) Tj
T* (subsidy and claim the remaining technical salary under federal R&D tax credits \(IRS Section 41 or SR&ED\) for a further 20–35%) Tj
T* (recovery, \(3\) Use regional equipment grants \(e.g. NJEDA or provincial vouchers\) to cover 50% of hardware and machinery capex, and) Tj
T* (\(4\) Secure low-cost debt \(SBA 7a / 504 or BDC\) to fund the remaining cash-share.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
45.354330708661422 645.1655905511810261 Td
(AUDIT SAFEGUARD: Never submit the same employee hours or invoice receipt to two separate grant reimbursement claims. Each) Tj
T* (grant agreement must have an isolated, non-overlapping work package.) Tj
ET
